{
  "version": 205,
  "released": "2026-08-24",
  "changelog": "v205: cross-dating \u2014 a resolved anchor places its dependent moments. WHY: the owner filed his birth landmark on staging (1981-07-11, day, basis stated) after keystones() promised \"one answer would place 53 more things\" \u2014 and the moment \"Born in Redlands while the family lived in the area\" still read UNDATED, still carrying a stale free-text anchor: dad attending ASU that was not even temporally right (ASU came later). ROOT CAUSE: nothing in the package had ever propagated a resolved anchor to its dependent moments. A date reached a moment through exactly two doors \u2014 the classifier's own events[].date claim, and an explicit per-moment timeline-place. from_age, from_anchor, intersect and the whole anchor index were reachable but had no caller that walked the undated moments and tried them, so the leverage number promised what no pass delivered. FIX: (1) system/cross_dating.py \u2014 a pure, stateless derivation-time pass invoked by timeline_data() between place_events and build_bands, trying one derivation per still-undated moment, strongest join first: DEFINITIONAL (the moment IS a landmark fact \u2014 birth, a move as a residence-span boundary, a graduation as a schooling-span end, or the classifier's own anchor field when it resolves through chronology.anchor_key to an indexed landmark EXACTLY), then an explicit AGE STATEMENT against the birthday (parse_age is greedy by design, so the pass hands it only what an age statement matched \u2014 \"at 19 I left home\" yes, \"the house at 19 Elm Street\" no), then CONTAINMENT, which reads a known place or era span as a terminus post/ante quem pair \u2014 bounds, never a point, the place join on the same provable source overlap _place_for_event uses. Markers are small, explicit and per-field; somebody else's birth in the same sentence vetoes the birth join outright; a free-text anchor naming nothing derives nothing. A miss is fine, a wrong join is not. (2) FOUR INVARIANTS: an explicit record is never overwritten; nothing is invented; every derived date names the landmark it leaned on and renders that provenance (\"from your birthday\") where the classifier's anchor used to sit, demoting the model's own note to the detail line rather than deleting it; and NO STATE \u2014 derived dates live only in the derived payload, so correcting a landmark re-derives everything instantly and there is nothing to migrate or repair. Confidence is graded by join tightness: inferred for definitional and place, conjectural for era (the documentary editors' mark), so claim_score ranks them correctly for free. (3) LEVERAGE HONESTY: dependency_index's MOMENT claims are now computed by cross_dating.derivable_moments \u2014 the pass's own containment rule read backwards \u2014 so the promise and the delivery come from the same join. Two fictions went away: a dated EVENT no longer claims its undated neighbours (a point is not a span) and a PERSON entity no longer claims the moments sharing its sources (an arrival bounds nothing); each keeps what is definitional (an era's bounds, the era_gaps it closes, the place_span rows a dated era's moments transitively fill via _place_span, a place's own span). keystones(), dig_plan() and the greedy plan are untouched. (4) Unknowns shrink with no extra wiring: unknowns() reads event[\"date\"] off the payload the pass just wrote, and build_bands runs after it, so dating an era transitively closes the place_span unknowns inside it. FINDINGS: chronology gained three public names the pass needed (anchor_key, lookup_anchor, NUMBER_WORDS) with the private aliases kept, so the age detector and parse_age can never disagree about what counts as an age. A synthetic mirror of the founder vault's shape \u2014 48 Childhood moments across 48 answers \u2014 dates all 48 the moment the era gets a span. TESTS: tests/test_cross_dating.py (the owner's exact case as a golden, the wrong-join vetoes, an age statement, residence bounds, a conflicting explicit record NOT overwritten, and promise==delivery asserted on a synthetic vault).",
